Notes:
- Discover capabilities once with {action:"list", capabilities:true}, then reuse that result for this session's launches. Refresh after agent configuration changes/reloads or a capability mismatch, not before every invocation; launch preflight remains authoritative.
- Plan mode may launch read-only agents only. Writers and nested agents require execute mode.
- Children start with fresh context: state objective, scope, files and output format in the task. Pass context:"fork" only when the child should reason over what this session already read (for example a second review of the same diff).
- Completion arrives as a native notification; do not poll or wait just for a wake. Use bg_wait only when this turn cannot proceed without the result. Controls: status (fleet or transcript), interrupt, stop, steer; steering recovery is disabled.
- On launch or child infrastructure failure, stop that lane and report the exact failure, run status, cwd and branch/ref. Verify a clean worktree or capture its partial diff before retrying. Do not silently substitute another agent, model, protocol or execution mode.
